      en: "East Coast Park is a 185-hectare coastal park in eastern Singapore, stretching 15 km along the shoreline. Built on reclaimed land in the 1970s, it offers diverse recreational activities including cycling, inline skating, barbecue, picnicking, and water sports. A 7.5 km cycling and jogging path runs along the coast. The park features Marine Cove playground, restaurants, and East Coast Lagoon Food Village. The beach is popular for sunbathing and swimming. It is a key recreational area for locals and tourists.",
